Author:     Federico Carrone <mail@fcarrone.com>
AuthorDate: Sun Nov 8 06:06:48 2026 +0000
Commit:     Federico Carrone <mail@fcarrone.com>
CommitDate: Sun Nov 8 06:06:48 2026 +0000

    signoff: the cap comes from the class of the member's diff (docs 2, scripts 3, compiler/spec 5); the hook takes only real records in the notes tier (review round 1)
    
    Codex and Kimi (round 1): a sign-off was accepted without the member having reached its review cap
    (R-0618). The record now names `rounds-at`, the member's own review.sh-noted commit; verify needs
    --base and requires that note's rounds to reach the cap of the diff's class, by path, the highest class
    present winning (an unclassified path counts as compiler/spec). Controls: a docs-only member after 2
    rounds is accepted; a scripts member and a mixed docs+compiler member after 2 rounds are refused, by
    record (nothing written) and by verify.
    Codex and Kimi: hash-object without --no-filters could store bytes other than those hashed: fixed.
    Kimi: the hook trusted the ref name; a refs/owner-signoff/* push takes the notes tier only for a
    parentless commit under a 40-hex name whose tree is exactly the four files (controls: a source commit
    and a non-SHA name take the full tier).
    agy: pure_merge no longer pipes merge-tree into head (conflict detection without pipefail); record
    verifies before writing the ref; verify checks record.txt exists before reading it.
    Fixed by Claude directly (pinpointed findings on a branch that predates the writers rule, as agreed).
