• scripts/land/signoff.sh:159: reviewer outputs are not bound to the approved commit; they are only hashed and scanned for `VERDICT: ACCEPT`. After reviewing commit A, pass those same three files to `record` for commit B with a B-naming quote and sufficient rounds. Verification of B succeeds although Codex, Kimi and agy never reviewed B.

  scripts/land/signoff.sh:143: the cap check extracts the first `rounds:` line without validating that the note is a well-formed `review.sh` note. A note containing only `rounds: 5`, or one with duplicate keys that `scripts/review/verify.sh` rejects as malformed, satisfies the cap and allows the sign-off.

  scripts/land/signoff.sh:132: a seven-hex-digit quote prefix is accepted without checking uniqueness. If approved commit A and another commit B share that prefix, A’s owner quote can be copied into B’s record and passes the quote check even though the owner never approved B.

  .githooks/pre-push:54: the hook compares only root entry names, not entry types or modes. A parentless commit with four directories named `agy.txt`, `codex.txt`, `kimi.txt`, and `record.txt`, containing arbitrary source files beneath them, takes the no-gates tier when pushed under a 40-hex ref. The control at `scripts/checks/review_tool.sh:305` constructs only flat blobs, so it misses this source-carrying case.

